sequenceDiagram
    accTitle: Record, checkpoint, cold boot, and restore
    accDescr: A live world emits structural twins to Crystallizer, which records them and seals a checkpoint. Assets are stored locally or through caller handlers. A fresh process reloads, preflights, and rebuilds the world through normal runtime verbs before returning a report.

    actor App as Live application
    participant Crystal as Crystallizer
    participant Record as Persistence record
    participant Store as Cache / external store
    participant Fresh as Fresh process + RestoreEngine

    App->>Crystal: configure + activate
    App->>Crystal: bind / conjure / link lifecycle emits
    Crystal->>Record: replace current structural twins
    App->>Crystal: create_checkpoint()
    Crystal->>Record: seal profile window
    Record-->>Crystal: detached checkpoint
    Crystal->>Store: flush checkpoint
    Note over App,Store: original process ends
    Fresh->>Store: reload profile / newest checkpoint
    Store-->>Fresh: detached records
    Fresh->>Fresh: verify chain + preflight
    Fresh->>Fresh: rebuild via configure / bind / conjure / link
    Fresh-->>App: restore report + fresh runtime identities
